  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $t\\geq 1$ and $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ be such that whenever $a,b\\in A$ with $b-a\\geq t$ we have $b-a\nmid b$. How large can $\\lvert A\\rvert$ be? Is it true that $ \\lvert A\\rvert \\leq \\left(\\frac{1}{2}+o_t(1)\\right)N? $ ",
